The GMRF Approximation
\[
\begin{aligned}
\pi(\mathbf{x}\mid {\theta},\mathbf{y}) & \propto \pi(\mathbf{x}\mid {\theta}) \pi(\mathbf{y}|\mathbf{x},\theta) \\
& \propto \exp\left\{-\frac{1}{2}\mathbf{x}^T\mathbf{Q}\mathbf{x} + \sum \log \pi(y_i|\eta_i,\theta)\right\}\\
\end{aligned}
\]
\[
\begin{aligned}
& \approx \exp\left\{-\frac{1}{2}\mathbf{x}^T\mathbf{Q}\mathbf{x} + \sum (b_i\eta_i - \frac{1}{2}c_i\eta_i^2)\right\}
\end{aligned}
\]
Recall \[
\begin{aligned}
        f(x) \approx f(x_0) + f'(x_0)(x-x_0)+ \frac{1}{2} f''(x_0)(x-x_0)^2
        = a+ bx - \frac{1}{2}cx^2
\end{aligned}
\] with
\[
\begin{aligned}
b &=f'(x_0) - f''(x_0)x_0\\
c &= -f''(x_0)
\end{aligned}
\].

The GMFR approximation - One dimensional example


Assume \[
\begin{aligned}
  y|\lambda \sim\text{Poisson}(\lambda)  & \text{ Likelihood}\\
  \eta = \log(\lambda)  & \text{ Predictor}\\
  \mathbf{x}  = \eta & \text{ Latent field }\\
  x\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1) & \text{ Latent Model}
\end{aligned}
\] we have that
\[
\begin{aligned}
  \pi(x|y) & \propto\pi(y|x)\pi(x)\\
  & \propto\exp\{ -\frac{1}{2}x^2+
  \underbrace{xy-\exp(x)}_{\text{non-gaussian part}}
  \}
\end{aligned}
\]

The Laplace Approximation
\[
\pi(\mathbf{\theta} \mid \mathbf{y}) \propto \frac{
            \overbrace{\pi( \mathbf{y}\mid \mathbf{x},\mathbf{\theta})\  \pi(\mathbf{\theta})}^{\text{Non-Gaussian, KNOWN}}  \overbrace{\pi( \mathbf{x}\mid \mathbf{\theta})}^{\text{ Gaussian}}  }
            {\underbrace{\pi(\mathbf{x} \mid \mathbf{y},
            \mathbf{\theta})}_{\text{Non-Gaussian,UNKNOWN}}}\: \Bigg|_{\text{For any value of } \mathbf{x}}
\]

The Laplace Approximation
\[
\begin{aligned}
\pi(\mathbf{\theta} \mid  \mathbf{y})  & \propto \frac{
            \pi( \mathbf{y}\mid \mathbf{x},\mathbf{\theta})\  \pi(\mathbf{\theta})  \pi( \mathbf{x}\mid \mathbf{\theta})  }
            {\pi(\mathbf{x} \mid \mathbf{y},
            \mathbf{\theta})} \: \Bigg|_{\text{For any value of } \mathbf{x}}\\
            & \approx \frac{
            \pi( \mathbf{y}\mid \mathbf{x},\mathbf{\theta})\  \pi(\mathbf{\theta})  \pi( \mathbf{x}\mid \mathbf{\theta})  }
            {\color{red}{\pi_G(\mathbf{x} \mid \mathbf{y},
            \mathbf{\theta})}}\: \Bigg|_{\text{Accuracy depends on the value of } \mathbf{x}}
\end{aligned}
\]

The Laplace Approximation


\[
\begin{aligned}
\pi(\mathbf{\theta} \mid  \mathbf{y})  & \propto \frac{
            \pi( \mathbf{y}\mid \mathbf{x},\mathbf{\theta})\  \pi(\mathbf{\theta})  \pi( \mathbf{x}\mid \mathbf{\theta})  }
            {\pi(\mathbf{x} \mid \mathbf{y},
            \mathbf{\theta})}\\
            & \approx \frac{
            \pi( \mathbf{y}\mid \mathbf{x},\mathbf{\theta})\  \pi(\mathbf{\theta})  \pi( \mathbf{x}\mid \mathbf{\theta})  }
            {\pi_G(\mathbf{x} \mid \mathbf{y},
            \mathbf{\theta})}  \: \Bigg|_{\mathbf{x} = \mathbf{x}^\star(\mathbf{\theta})}
\end{aligned}
\]
If \(\theta\) is low dimension we can actually compute this!











This is the Laplace approximation to \(\pi(\theta|\mathbf{y})\) !

The Laplace approximation….again!
\[
\begin{aligned}
\pi(x_i|\mathbf{y}) & \propto \frac{\pi(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y},\theta)}{\pi(\mathbf{x}_{-i}\mid x_i,\theta,
\mathbf{y})}\: \Bigg|_{\text{For any value of } \mathbf{x}_{-i} \text{ and } \theta} \\
& \approx  \frac{\pi(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y},\theta)}{\color{red}{\pi_{GG}(\mathbf{x}_{-i}\mid x_i,\theta,
\mathbf{y})}}\: \Bigg|_{\text{Accurancy depends on values of } \mathbf{x}_{-i} \text{ and } \theta}
\end{aligned}
\]
\(\pi_{GG}(\mathbf{x}_{-i}\mid x_i,\theta,\mathbf{y})\) is the Gaussian approximation to \(\mathbf{x}_{-i}\mid x_i,\theta,\mathbf{y}\)

The Laplace approximation….again!
\[
\begin{aligned}
\pi(x_i|\mathbf{y}) & \propto \frac{\pi(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y},\theta)}{\pi(\mathbf{x}_{-i}\mid x_i,\theta,
\mathbf{y})}\: \Bigg|_{\text{For any value of } \mathbf{x}_{-i} \text{ and } \theta} \\
& \approx  \frac{\pi(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y},\theta)}{\color{red}{\pi_{GG}(\mathbf{x}_{-i}\mid x_i,\theta,
\mathbf{y})}}\: \Bigg|_{\mathbf{x}_{-i} = \mathbf{x}_{-i}^*(x_i,\theta)}
\end{aligned}
\]
